      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T02:58:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 57: 🔴 The increase coalescing can apply an immediate bitrate increase after exactly one unchanged sample, because `lastTargetChange_` is updated only when the target changes. In practice, if congestion control reports 2200 twice after 2000, the second call after a short interval passes the `targetChanged || now - lastTargetChange_ \u003c STABILITY_DELAY` condition once the delay since the first target change has elapsed, even though stability at that target may not have been established by repeated samples. Track when the same target has remained stable, or require `now - lastTargetChange_ \u003e\u003d STABILITY_DELAY` regardless of `targetChanged`.",
      "revId": "80ed001ed77cf5cf771d621c24b90f98ac74b257",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
